Package: clickclick
Version: 0.1
Title: Keyboard and Mouse Input Simulation for macOS
Description: Control your keyboard and mouse with R code by simulating mouse
    moves, clicks, drags, key presses, and typed text. The input simulation
    is implemented in Objective-C using macOS's CoreGraphics event APIs,
    built on top of the open-source 'cliclick' command-line tool
    <https://github.com/BlueM/cliclick>, compiled directly into the package
    and invoked in-process rather than as a subprocess.
Author: Rubemaster [aut, cre], Carsten Bluem [aut, cph] (Author of the bundled 'cliclick' source)
Maintainer: Rubemaster <RGRICK2@illinois.edu>
License: file LICENSE
OS_type: mac
SystemRequirements: macOS
URL: https://github.com/Rubemaster/clickclick
BugReports: https://github.com/Rubemaster/clickclick/issues
NeedsCompilation: yes
